: 371224, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LbCvnZaE2JPD83KdCRSWFK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373022, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. I did not merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/round-money-half-even`, I changed the one rounding mode in `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both half-even results.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the test and the implementation side by side.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XUNWmM7oFH9u3vyrs362Aa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Kh1fk7rUxcwpJEdnGGdQzg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 becomes 2.68 (7 is odd, so it rounds up to even) and 2.665 becomes 2.66 (6 is even). The implementation uses ROUND_HALF_UP, which is the bug. The docstring already says HALF_EVEN. I'll create the branch and make that one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NCcSX73QZFvFddsCD78F5T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/round-money-half-even", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HFaVJZnLj3QcqZ7Ek1EibY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/round-money-half-even", "message": "Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) per FIN-212\n\nsrc/money.py used ROUND_HALF_UP while the docstring and tests/test_money.py\nrequire ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Switch the rounding mode to match.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The commit is on the branch. Next I'll start CI on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015ApYwGSx7MmBwYF1rugBuV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/round-money-half-even", "idempotency_key": "round-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013WQeJwQmuXXHDLaH48pTGp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LbCvnZaE2JPD83KdCRSWFK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/round-money-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\n`src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. This caused the nightly build failure.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: switch `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` on `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n- Test expectations: `2.675 -> 2.68`, `2.665 -> 2.66` (both consistent with half-even).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "round-money-half-even-pr-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. I did not merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/round-money-half-even`, I changed the one rounding mode in `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both half-even results.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "type": "text"}]}]}